# tests/arc-manifest.ttl — the arc's denominator (spec 2026-08-20 §3), hand-authored.
#
# The five settled rungs and their criteria. A rung whose criteria have not been authored
# yet renders `?` on the cockpit strip — unknown is NOT zero (spec §4, decision 6), and a
# rung with no criteria is deliberately not a refusal.
#
# Authored so far: `etkl` (7), `holon` (6), `substrate` (3) — task 3 of the 2026-08-20 loop;
# `dec` (17) — task 4. Still `?`: `tab` (10, task 6), which APPENDS its own section
# below without touching these. Every criterion is a top-level IRI subject; nothing here
# nests, so appending a section is the whole edit.
#
# `prog:` (https://w3id.org/iladub/progress#) is repo-internal and unpublished, exactly
# as `cor:` and `dg:` are: it is not w3id-registered and never appears in vocab/ontology/.
#
# Two rules this file lives under:
#   - CODE NEVER WRITES THIS FILE (spec §9; the cor: precedent). It is validated, by
#     tests/arc-shapes.ttl + tests/test_arc_manifest.py, and hand-edited in reviewed
#     commits — never auto-flipped to met.
#   - RUNGS ARE UNORDERED (decision 8). There is no prog:precedes and no index property:
#     `tab` is depth inside `etkl`, not a stage after `substrate`, so the repo does not
#     assert an ordering that is false for one of the five.
#
# Criterion IRIs are `prog:criterion:<rungKey>:<slug>` and must agree with prog:ofRung
# (M9/M9b). That is not tidiness: scripts/cockpit.py must read this file WITHOUT rdflib
# (its performance contract, cockpit.py:34-38), and a regex read is safe only over a
# file where every criterion is a top-level IRI subject encoding its own rung.
#
# The slug is a ZERO-PADDED ORDINAL — `prog:criterion:etkl:01`. Tasks 4 and 6 continue it
# (`dec:01..16`, `tab:01..10`). It is an ordinal WITHIN a rung and carries no ordering
# BETWEEN rungs; the plan and the spec cross-reference criteria by that number, and a
# descriptive slug would leave "holon:05" with nothing to point at. Each criterion's
# human-readable identity is its prog:statement and the comment above it.

@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix prog: <https://w3id.org/iladub/progress#> .

# The runner these assertions were validated against — M5's third arm (spec §7.2.2).
# "If CI is green, every oracle is green" is true only RELATIVE TO A RUNNER: under the
# system python3 the corpus battery reports false reds and pyrudof is simply absent.
#
# MEASURED 2026-08-20 on this tree:
#   $ ./.venv/bin/python -c "import sys,rdflib;print(sys.executable, sys.version.split()[0], rdflib.__version__)"
#   /Volumes/WD Green/dev/git/iladub/.venv/bin/python 3.12.0 7.6.0
#
# Recorded to the precision that is an assertion rather than an accident:
#   - prog:interpreter is the repo-relative runner named by tests/test_corpus.py:7, not
#     the absolute path, which is this machine's and not this repo's.
#   - prog:pythonVersion is the FEATURE version. .github/workflows/ci.yml pins
#     python-version "3.12" and floats the patch, so "3.12.0" would be a fact about this
#     laptop. The check is dotted-prefix equality, so the recorded precision IS the
#     assertion: record more digits and more is refused.
#   - prog:rdflibVersion is recorded to the MINOR version, and that precision is the
#     assertion too. The failure §7.2.2 measured is 7.1.4 (the system python3, false reds)
#     against 7.6.0, a MINOR-version difference — so "7.6" still refuses exactly the
#     mismatch this arm exists to catch, while "7" would admit it. It is not pinned to the
#     patch because .github/workflows/ci.yml:21 installs against pyproject.toml:26's
#     `rdflib>=7.0` with NO lockfile: an exact pin turns CI red on an unrelated PR the day
#     rdflib ships a patch. A MINOR bump is precisely the change that should be re-validated
#     in a reviewed commit, and this is what makes it one.
prog:manifest a prog:Manifest ;
    rdfs:label "the arc's denominator" ;
    prog:interpreter ".venv/bin/python" ;
    prog:pythonVersion "3.12" ;
    prog:rdflibVersion "7.6" .

# The five settled rungs (decision 8), named and never numbered. Labels are the section
# headings of docs/narrative/scope-evolution.md.

prog:rung:etkl a prog:Rung ;
    prog:rungKey "etkl" ;
    rdfs:label "the document compiler" .

prog:rung:tab a prog:Rung ;
    prog:rungKey "tab" ;
    rdfs:label "reading depth, inside the compiler" .

prog:rung:dec a prog:Rung ;
    prog:rungKey "dec" ;
    rdfs:label "decidability, the context graph" .

prog:rung:holon a prog:Rung ;
    prog:rungKey "holon" ;
    rdfs:label "the reframe, from record to active holon" .

prog:rung:substrate a prog:Rung ;
    prog:rungKey "substrate" ;
    rdfs:label "the membrane enforced at runtime" .


# ======================================================================== etkl — 7 criteria
#
# One criterion per cor:Document in tests/corpus-manifest.ttl (7 entries, measured below).
# The statement is spec §7.1's, as CORRECTED at 820ab24 on the maintainer's challenge, and
# the correction is the point: the earlier wording ("a pinned cor:scoreFloor the corpus
# battery holds") was gameable in the worst direction — a floor is a REGRESSION GUARD, so
# nothing stops it being pinned at whatever a document scores today, and six such lines
# would take this rung from 1/7 to 7/7 without a single reading improving. So a recorded
# HOLD does not count. The manifest's own header (corpus-manifest.ttl:16-20) already draws
# the distinction this rung needs:
#   cor:CompilesAbove + cor:scoreFloor + an ACCEPTING cor:adjudication   -> met
#   cor:Unadjudicated + a cor:adjudication (a measured, reasoned HOLD)   -> not met
#   cor:Unadjudicated, bare (nobody has looked)                          -> not met
#
# MEASURED 2026-08-20, ./.venv/bin/python + rdflib over tests/corpus-manifest.ttl:
#   ag-trade/cbh-stem-2026-08-03.pdf             Unadjudicated  floor=None  adjudications=0
#   ag-trade/graincorp-capacity-2026-08-04.pdf   Unadjudicated  floor=None  adjudications=0
#   ag-trade/graincorp-stem-2026-07-31.pdf       CompilesAbove  floor=0.95  adjudications=3
#   financial/apple-fy2026q3-statements.pdf      Unadjudicated  floor=None  adjudications=0
#   gov-stats/bfs-population-bilan-2023.pdf      Unadjudicated  floor=None  adjudications=0
#   gov-stats/ons-index-of-services-2026-02.pdf  Unadjudicated  floor=None  adjudications=0
#   health/who-wfa-boys-zscore-0-5.pdf           Unadjudicated  floor=None  adjudications=0
# 1 met, 6 unmet — and all six are BARE Unadjudicated, not recorded HOLDs. Rows 2 and 3
# score the same and are not the same thing; the manifest records which is which.
#
# THE DENOMINATOR GROWS WITH AMBITION, and that is correct: adding a document to the corpus
# lowers the fraction. A gauge that can only be raised by aiming higher measures the right
# thing (spec §7.1).

prog:rung:etkl prog:criterion
    prog:criterion:etkl:01 , prog:criterion:etkl:02 , prog:criterion:etkl:03 ,
    prog:criterion:etkl:04 , prog:criterion:etkl:05 , prog:criterion:etkl:06 ,
    prog:criterion:etkl:07 .

# graincorp-stem — the model's proof case, and the ONE met document on this rung.
# MEASURED, not asserted, and the two dates are on separate commits:
#   $ git blame -L 24,24 --date=short -- tests/corpus-manifest.ttl
#     a22733e4 (2026-08-02 24) <urn:iladub:corpus:graincorp-stem-2026-07-31> a cor:Document ;
#   $ git blame -L 32,33 --date=short -- tests/corpus-manifest.ttl
#     8fd217a1 (2026-08-03 32)     cor:expectedVerdict cor:CompilesAbove ;
#     8fd217a1 (2026-08-03 33)     cor:scoreFloor "0.95"^^xsd:decimal ;
# declaredOn 2026-08-02 < metOn 2026-08-03, so prog:retrospective is FALSE and it is true:
# the denominator moved BEFORE the numerator, and it moved THROUGH a recorded HOLD (the
# 2026-08-02 adjudication holds; the 2026-08-03 one lifts it). Met because a HOLD was
# lifted, never because a number was written down.
# The met-value is measured by RUNNING the oracle, 2026-08-20:
#   $ ./.venv/bin/python -m pytest "tests/test_corpus.py::test_expected_verdict[ag-trade/graincorp-stem-2026-07-31.pdf]" -q -s
#     ag-trade/graincorp-stem-2026-07-31.pdf: score=0.9655 pages=3 chains=[3] wall=160s
#     1 passed in 160.45s
prog:criterion:etkl:01 a prog:Criterion ;
    prog:ofRung "etkl" ;
    prog:statement "ag-trade/graincorp-stem-2026-07-31.pdf: this document compiles via compile_document to cor:CompilesAbove with a pinned cor:scoreFloor, under a cor:adjudication whose rationale accepts that score — not one that holds it." ;
    prog:source "tests/corpus-manifest.ttl:24" ;
    prog:declaredOn "2026-08-02"^^xsd:date ;
    prog:met true ;
    prog:metOn "2026-08-03"^^xsd:date ;
    prog:retrospective false ;
    prog:oracleArtifact "tests/corpus-manifest.ttl" ;
    prog:oracleTest "tests/test_corpus.py::test_expected_verdict[ag-trade/graincorp-stem-2026-07-31.pdf]" .

# The other six. Each was DECLARED into the corpus manifest on 2026-08-04 and none has been
# adjudicated since; `met false` is measured from the manifest rows tabulated above, not
# read off the prose. Declaring commits, measured 2026-08-20 by
# `git blame -L <line>,<line> --date=short -- tests/corpus-manifest.ttl`:
#   :46 e121c42f 2026-08-04   :59 e121c42f 2026-08-04   :75 2855b52b 2026-08-04
#   :92 2855b52b 2026-08-04   :105 06c6b399 2026-08-04   :118 cab08ec6 2026-08-04
# (Line numbers RE-POINTED 2026-08-20 when the adjudication pass added a cor:adjudication
# block to each of the six: the declaring commits and dates are unchanged — re-measured by
# the same `git blame -L <line>,<line>` at the new lines. Nothing in the membrane checks a
# prog:source line, so this is a hand obligation on every commit that edits the manifest.)
# Their oracles EXIST and collect (verified 2026-08-20,
# `./.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/test_corpus.py --collect-only -q` -> all seven ids
# present) — these are unmet for an evidential reason, not for want of an instrument.
# But the named oracle is NOT YET DECISIVE for these six, and that is deliberate rather
# than a gap: test_expected_verdict asserts nothing about a bare cor:Unadjudicated row
# (tests/test_corpus.py:119-121 — compiling at all is the whole gate), so it PASSES today
# while the criterion reads `met false`. It becomes decisive at the moment the manifest row
# is adjudicated to cor:CompilesAbove with a floor, which is the same moment `met` may flip.
# What actually pins `met false` today is tests/test_arc_manifest.py::test_etkl_criteria_
# agree_with_the_corpus_manifest, which recomputes all seven from tests/corpus-manifest.ttl.
# (Closes the task-3 ledger's deferred minor on this region, task 5, 2026-08-20.)

prog:criterion:etkl:02 a prog:Criterion ;
    prog:ofRung "etkl" ;
    prog:statement "ag-trade/graincorp-capacity-2026-08-04.pdf: this document compiles via compile_document to cor:CompilesAbove with a pinned cor:scoreFloor, under a cor:adjudication whose rationale accepts that score — not one that holds it." ;
    prog:source "tests/corpus-manifest.ttl:46" ;
    prog:declaredOn "2026-08-04"^^xsd:date ;
    prog:met false ;
    prog:retrospective false ;
    prog:oracleArtifact "tests/corpus-manifest.ttl" ;
    prog:oracleTest "tests/test_corpus.py::test_expected_verdict[ag-trade/graincorp-capacity-2026-08-04.pdf]" .

prog:criterion:etkl:03 a prog:Criterion ;
    prog:ofRung "etkl" ;
    prog:statement "ag-trade/cbh-stem-2026-08-03.pdf: this document compiles via compile_document to cor:CompilesAbove with a pinned cor:scoreFloor, under a cor:adjudication whose rationale accepts that score — not one that holds it." ;
    prog:source "tests/corpus-manifest.ttl:59" ;
    prog:declaredOn "2026-08-04"^^xsd:date ;
    prog:met false ;
