# ======================================================================= holon — 6 criteria
#
# Read off docs/holonic-interaction.md, which states BOTH halves — § "What is built"
# (4 bullets, :147-156) and § "Planned work (not done yet)" (2 bullets, :160-163). A page
# that says what it has NOT done is a denominator; a page that lists only what shipped is a
# changelog. Line numbers re-verified 2026-08-20:
#   $ grep -n -e "What is built" -e "Planned work" docs/holonic-interaction.md
#     145:## What is built
#     158:## Planned work (not done yet)
#
# ALL SIX carry prog:declaredOn "2026-06-23" — 781527f, `feat(holons): align iladub to W3C
# Holon CG / HGA + grounding governance`. MEASURED 2026-08-20:
#   $ git blame -L 147,156 --date=short -- docs/holonic-interaction.md
#     781527ff 2026-06-23 for :149-156 ; d0b3e557 2026-07-01 for :147-148
#   $ git blame -L 160,163 --date=short -- docs/holonic-interaction.md
#     781527ff 2026-06-23 for :160, :162-163 ; d0b3e557 2026-07-01 for :161
# The 2026-07-01 touches are the `iladub:`->`etkl:` namespace RENAME and nothing else
# (`git show 781527f:docs/holonic-interaction.md` has the same bullet naming
# `vocab/ontology/iladub-holons.ttl`), and a rename is not a re-declaration — the same rule
# the plan applies to dec:16. Going back further, `git show 0597988:docs/holonic-interaction.md`
# (2026-06-02, the file-creating commit) has NO "What is built" section at all and a
# DIFFERENT "Planned work" list, so the section content was fully replaced at 781527f.
#
# The four met ones are prog:retrospective TRUE, and that is a MEASUREMENT rather than a
# convention: `git log --diff-filter=A` puts iladub-hga-align.ttl, iladub-hga-shapes.ttl,
# holon-grounding-conformant.ttl, holon-grounding-leak.ttl and test_hga_alignment.py ALL at
# 781527f — the bullets and the artifacts they describe landed in the SAME commit, so
# metOn == declaredOn and M4 refuses `retrospective false` outright. The clause fires on
# real data here, not on a fixture.
# (etkl-holons.ttl's own --diff-filter=A is 3433fd0 2026-07-01, which is the file MOVE that
# renamed iladub-holons.ttl; the content it describes landed at 781527f with the rest.)
#
# The two unmet ones are prog:retrospective FALSE — declared ahead of the evidence — so
# flipping either is a real measurement and not an adjudication. Their oracles are TARGETS
# that do not exist yet, which is permitted (spec §3): M5/M5b bite only on `met true`.
#
# Note what this rung's fraction refutes: CLAUDE.md § Open items still says this work is
# "not yet started". The rung reads 4/6. The instrument's first act is to contradict the
# Contract file — which is the instrument working (spec §7.3).

prog:rung:holon prog:criterion
    prog:criterion:holon:01 , prog:criterion:holon:02 , prog:criterion:holon:03 ,
    prog:criterion:holon:04 , prog:criterion:holon:05 , prog:criterion:holon:06 .

# MEASURED 2026-08-20 for criteria 01-04:
#   $ ./.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/test_hga_alignment.py -q
#     ......                                                              [100%]
#     6 passed in 0.32s
# and every named artifact is on disk (`ls -la` on the five paths, all present).

prog:criterion:holon:01 a prog:Criterion ;
    prog:ofRung "holon" ;
    prog:statement "vocab/ontology/etkl-holons.ttl — the holon types + grounding portal + membrane health, in the etkl namespace, standalone (no HGA dependency)." ;
    prog:source "docs/holonic-interaction.md:147-148" ;
    prog:declaredOn "2026-06-23"^^xsd:date ;
    prog:met true ;
    prog:metOn "2026-06-23"^^xsd:date ;
    prog:retrospective true ;
    prog:oracleArtifact "vocab/ontology/etkl-holons.ttl" ;
    prog:oracleTest "tests/test_hga_alignment.py::test_holons_module_standalone" .

# The second oracle is deliberate: test_alignment_axioms_present pins that the alignment
# axioms ARE there, and test_alignment_modules_only_point_outward pins the other half of
# "alignment-not-import" — every subject in the module is a term we own (CLAUDE.md
# § Source ownership). One test alone would leave half the statement unpinned.
prog:criterion:holon:02 a prog:Criterion ;
    prog:ofRung "holon" ;
    prog:statement "vocab/ontology/iladub-hga-align.ttl — the optional HGA alignment (alignment-not-import): rdfs:subClassOf axioms only, pointing our document holons and grounding portal outward at the HGA substrate classes and never importing them." ;
    prog:source "docs/holonic-interaction.md:149-150" ;
    prog:declaredOn "2026-06-23"^^xsd:date ;
    prog:met true ;
    prog:metOn "2026-06-23"^^xsd:date ;
    prog:retrospective true ;
    prog:oracleArtifact "vocab/ontology/iladub-hga-align.ttl" ;
    prog:oracleTest "tests/test_hga_alignment.py::test_alignment_axioms_present" ;
    prog:oracleTest "tests/test_source_ownership.py::test_alignment_modules_only_point_outward" .

prog:criterion:holon:03 a prog:Criterion ;
    prog:ofRung "holon" ;
    prog:statement "vocab/shapes/iladub-hga-shapes.ttl — iladub:HgaGroundingGovernanceShape: an HGA GroundingRecord may reach RegisteredStatus only as the product of an iladub:PromotionDecision (iladub's invariant layered onto HGA's bare confidence gate)." ;
    prog:source "docs/holonic-interaction.md:151-153" ;
    prog:declaredOn "2026-06-23"^^xsd:date ;
    prog:met true ;
    prog:metOn "2026-06-23"^^xsd:date ;
    prog:retrospective true ;
    prog:oracleArtifact "vocab/shapes/iladub-hga-shapes.ttl" ;
    prog:oracleTest "tests/test_hga_alignment.py::test_governed_grounding_conformant" ;
    prog:oracleTest "tests/test_hga_alignment.py::test_ungoverned_grounding_rejected" .

prog:criterion:holon:04 a prog:Criterion ;
    prog:ofRung "holon" ;
    prog:statement "examples/holon-grounding-conformant.ttl + tests/holon-grounding-leak.ttl — a conforming governed-grounding traversal and a negative case; exercised by tests/test_hga_alignment.py." ;
    prog:source "docs/holonic-interaction.md:154-156" ;
    prog:declaredOn "2026-06-23"^^xsd:date ;
    prog:met true ;
    prog:metOn "2026-06-23"^^xsd:date ;
    prog:retrospective true ;
    prog:oracleArtifact "examples/holon-grounding-conformant.ttl" ;
    prog:oracleArtifact "tests/holon-grounding-leak.ttl" ;
    prog:oracleTest "tests/test_hga_alignment.py::test_governed_grounding_conformant" ;
    prog:oracleTest "tests/test_hga_alignment.py::test_ungoverned_grounding_rejected" .

# `met false` MEASURED 2026-08-20, not read off the "not done yet" heading:
#   $ grep -rn "membraneHealth\|MembraneHealth" src/ --include='*.py' | grep -v __pycache__
#     (no output — nothing in the compiler computes it)
