# =================================================================== substrate — 3 criteria
#
# THE ONE HONEST ZERO ON THE STRIP, and it must stay earned. All three are `met false` and
# all three are prog:retrospective FALSE — declared 2026-07-03, ahead of any evidence.
#
# ONE SENTENCE, THREE REQUIREMENTS. docs/narrative/scope-evolution.md:99-101 reads:
#   "A holon is only *active* if something **enforces its membrane at runtime**. That
#    requires an immutable **event ledger** (memory), **validation-at-write** (sensory), and
#    **in-engine policy** (motor)."
# All three criteria therefore carry the SAME prog:source and the SAME prog:declaredOn.
# Fabricating three distinct declaring lines would make them look independently declared,
# and they were not (spec §11 seam 3).
#
# MEASURED 2026-08-20:
#   $ git blame -L 97,102 --date=short -- docs/narrative/scope-evolution.md
#     3b366094 2026-08-20  97) ### `substrate` — the membrane enforced at runtime
#     20c3be43 2026-07-03  99) A holon is only *active* if something **enforces its ...
#     20c3be43 2026-07-03 100) immutable **event ledger** (memory), **validation-at-write** ...
#     20c3be43 2026-07-03 101) (motor). The chosen substrate provides all three natively, ...
#   The HEADING at :97 was reworded 2026-08-20; the SENTENCE was not. declaredOn is the
#   sentence's date, 2026-07-03.
#
# `met false` RE-MEASURED 2026-08-20 rather than inherited from the handoff — an unmet
# criterion is still an assertion:
#   $ find src/iladub/fluree -type f | sort | xargs wc -l
#          3 src/iladub/fluree/__init__.py
#         16 src/iladub/fluree/f-modify-policy-template.jsonld
#         15 src/iladub/fluree/f-policy-template.jsonld
#         34 total                       <- two JSON-LD policy TEMPLATES and an __init__
#   $ wc -l src/iladub/etkl/writegate.py
#         70 src/iladub/etkl/writegate.py
#   $ grep -rn "requests\.\|httpx\|urllib.request\|aiohttp\|http://localhost" src/ --include='*.py'
#     (no output — ZERO server/runtime client code anywhere in src/)
#   $ grep -rn "ledger" src/ --include='*.py' | grep -v __pycache__
#     only adoption.build_ledger and its call sites in compile.py — that is the ADOPTION
#     TOKEN ledger (a coverage accounting over a page), NOT an immutable event ledger.
#   $ grep -rn "from .membrane import\|from . import membrane" src/ --include='*.py'
#     src/iladub/feed.py:608 , src/iladub/etkl/compile.py:511 , src/iladub/etkl/tiling.py:69
#     — every membrane.validate call runs IN THE COMPILER PROCESS, on an in-memory Graph.
#   $ grep -rn "f-policy-template\|f-modify-policy-template" --include='*.py' .
#     src/iladub/etkl/federate.py:26 and two tests — the templates are PARSED by rdflib for
#     structural checks; nothing deploys them to an engine, and there is no engine.
#
# So: no ledger, no write endpoint, no engine. Three zeroes, each measured. The
# prog:oracleTest on each is a TARGET that does not exist yet (permitted, spec §3; M5b
# bites only on `met true`) — it names where the proof would have to live.

prog:rung:substrate prog:criterion
    prog:criterion:substrate:01 , prog:criterion:substrate:02 ,
    prog:criterion:substrate:03 .

prog:criterion:substrate:01 a prog:Criterion ;
    prog:ofRung "substrate" ;
    prog:statement "The membrane is enforced at runtime by an immutable event ledger (memory): the holon's history is kept by the substrate itself, not reconstructed by the compiler process." ;
    prog:source "docs/narrative/scope-evolution.md:99-101" ;
    prog:declaredOn "2026-07-03"^^xsd:date ;
    prog:met false ;
    prog:retrospective false ;
    prog:oracleTest "tests/substrate/test_event_ledger.py::test_committed_events_are_immutable" .

prog:criterion:substrate:02 a prog:Criterion ;
    prog:ofRung "substrate" ;
    prog:statement "The membrane is enforced at runtime by validation-at-write (sensory): a non-conforming write is refused AT THE WRITE ENDPOINT, not inside the process that produced it." ;
    prog:source "docs/narrative/scope-evolution.md:99-101" ;
    prog:declaredOn "2026-07-03"^^xsd:date ;
    prog:met false ;
    prog:retrospective false ;
    prog:oracleTest "tests/substrate/test_write_gate.py::test_engine_refuses_an_ungoverned_commit" .

prog:criterion:substrate:03 a prog:Criterion ;
    prog:ofRung "substrate" ;
    prog:statement "The membrane is enforced at runtime by in-engine policy (motor): access policy is evaluated by the engine on every read and write, not held in a template this repo only parses." ;
    prog:source "docs/narrative/scope-evolution.md:99-101" ;
    prog:declaredOn "2026-07-03"^^xsd:date ;
    prog:met false ;
    prog:retrospective false ;
    prog:oracleTest "tests/substrate/test_in_engine_policy.py::test_engine_enforces_ai_inherits_user" .


# ========================================================================= dec — 17 criteria
#
# THE DENOMINATOR WAS ALREADY WRITTEN DOWN, in this repo's Contract file. CLAUDE.md:252:
#   "Every vocabulary/shape ships with a worked example that conforms **and** a negative
#    test that must fail."
# That is a countable rule, and it has exactly ONE commit in its history — it has never been
# reworded since the day it was written. MEASURED 2026-08-21:
#   $ git log -L 252,252:CLAUDE.md --date=short --format='%h %ad %s'
#     ee221de 2026-05-31 Add CLAUDE.md and reference docs; wire up MkDocs nav
#     (one commit, the file-creating one; no later touch)
# So all SIXTEEN pairing criteria carry prog:declaredOn "2026-05-31" and prog:source
# "CLAUDE.md:252". The seventeenth criterion is a different rule and carries its own source.
#
# THE SHAPE CENSUS — the denominator, measured rather than inherited. Every sh:NodeShape in
# the four namespaces this rung governs (dec: / risk: / iladub: / gsh:), found by parsing
# every tracked .ttl with rdflib (not by grep — a shape declared across two lines would hide
# from grep), 2026-08-21:
#   vocab/shapes/dec-shapes.ttl         dec:DecisionHolonShape:15 dec:ConfidenceShape:38
#                                       dec:MilestoneShape:48 dec:EventShape:60
#                                       dec:ExpansionRequestShape:71
#   vocab/shapes/escalation-shapes.ttl  dec:EscalationShape:16
#   vocab/shapes/iladub-shapes.ttl      iladub:CandidateConceptShape:16
#                                       iladub:GroundedNodeShape:37
#                                       iladub:PromotionDecisionShape:53
#                                       iladub:NoLeakShape:65
#   vocab/shapes/risk-shapes.ttl        risk:NoEmpiricRiskShape:17
#                                       risk:RiskAssessmentShape:35 risk:SensitivityShape:49
#   vocab/shapes/governance-shapes.ttl  gsh:AiInheritsUserShape:27 gsh:PermissionShape:45
#   vocab/shapes/iladub-hga-shapes.ttl  iladub:HgaGroundingGovernanceShape:27
# That is SIXTEEN node shapes, not the fifteen the spec §7.2 counted — the sixteenth being
# iladub:HgaGroundingGovernanceShape. ALL SIXTEEN ARE AUTHORED HERE (criteria 01-16).
#
# THE SIXTEENTH OVERLAPS `holon` ON PURPOSE, and that is settled (Ruling 12, 2026-08-21).
# Task 4 first excluded it, on the ground that prog:criterion:holon:03 and :04 above already
# cite examples/holon-grounding-conformant.ttl and tests/holon-grounding-leak.ttl. The ruling
# overturned that: THE RUNGS PARTITION DECLARING PROSE, NOT ARTIFACTS. holon:03's
# prog:source is docs/holonic-interaction.md:151-153 and it asks whether that shape's
# INVARIANT is built; criterion 16 below carries prog:source CLAUDE.md:252 and asks whether
# the shape SHIPS A CONFORMING EXAMPLE AND A NEGATIVE TEST. Two rules about one artifact is
# the design — evidence reuse across criteria is already everywhere in this file (etkl:01's
# corpus row, holon:03 and :04 sharing both oracles). Exempting a shape because another rung
# mentions it would be a curation rule CLAUDE.md:252 does not contain: the rule ranges over
# "Every vocabulary/shape", and a curated denominator is a fabricated numerator seen from the
# other side. So: 16 shapes, 16 pairing criteria, no exemption.
#
# THE PAIRINGS ARE MEASURED, NOT ASSUMED — this is the step the brief warned about, since a
# `*-leak.ttl` fixture need not belong to the shape whose name it resembles. Every negative
# fixture in the repo was validated against the UNION of the five shape files and the firing
# sh:sourceShape read out of the report graph (blank property shapes resolved to their owning
# node shape). MEASURED 2026-08-21, ./.venv/bin/python + pyshacl, inference="rdfs",
# advanced=True:
#   tests/dec-bad.ttl                             -> dec:DecisionHolonShape
#   examples/transplant/heart-timeline-leak.ttl   -> dec:MilestoneShape
#   examples/transplant/event-leak.ttl            -> dec:EventShape
#   tests/expansion-request-leak.ttl              -> dec:ExpansionRequestShape
#   examples/transplant/transplant-escalation-leak.ttl -> dec:EscalationShape
#   tests/risk-leak.ttl                           -> risk:NoEmpiricRiskShape
#   tests/transplant-governance-leak.ttl          -> gsh:AiInheritsUserShape
#   tests/leak-attempt.ttl                        -> iladub:CandidateConceptShape
#                                                    + iladub:NoLeakShape
#   tests/federation-projection-leak.ttl          -> iladub:PromotionDecisionShape
#                                                    + dec:DecisionHolonShape
# and the two negative graphs built IN CODE by tests/test_grounding.py:
#   ::test_neg_grounded_without_promotion_fails   -> iladub:GroundedNodeShape (alone)
#   ::test_neg_proposition_asserted_fails         -> iladub:CandidateConceptShape
#                                                    + iladub:NoLeakShape
# That sweep loaded the FIVE shape files above; the sixteenth shape lives in a sixth
# (vocab/shapes/iladub-hga-shapes.ttl), so tests/holon-grounding-leak.ttl came back clean
# from it and was measured separately, against the shape graph its own caller loads:
#   tests/holon-grounding-leak.ttl -> iladub:HgaGroundingGovernanceShape (alone) — see 16
#
# THE ONE PAIRING THAT LOOKS LIKE A MATCH AND IS NOT. tests/federation-projection-leak.ttl
# trips iladub:PromotionDecisionShape in that union sweep — a bare tx:leaked-decision typed
# iladub:PromotionDecision with neither iladub:reviews nor dec:decidedBy. But no test
# validates that fixture against iladub-shapes.ttl: tests/test_federation.py:47 loads
# vocab/shapes/etkl-shapes.ttl alone, and the assertion at :61 is about etkl:DocumentProjectionShape
# refusing an interior leak. Nothing SHIPS that refusal as PromotionDecisionShape's negative
# test, so criterion 09 is unmet. This is precisely the trap the brief named, and the answer
# came from reading the caller, not the fixture name.
#
# NOT ALL SIXTEEN ARE prog:retrospective FALSE — the brief's claim (made of fifteen), re-
# measured and refuted.
# The rule predates most of the shapes it governs, but two pairings landed on the SAME DAY as
# the rule itself. MEASURED 2026-08-21, `git log --diff-filter=A --follow --date=short`:
#   examples/proposal.ttl  examples/promotion.ttl  tests/leak-attempt.ttl
#   vocab/shapes/iladub-shapes.ttl                  -> all e48ebf2 2026-05-31
#   $ git log -S"def test_leak_rejected" --date=short --format='%h %ad' -- .  | tail -1
#     e48ebf2 2026-05-31
# so for iladub:CandidateConceptShape (07) and iladub:NoLeakShape (10),
# metOn == declaredOn == 2026-05-31 and M4 refuses `retrospective false` outright: the
# criterion was written against evidence that already existed. They are labelled TRUE, and
# labelling them is the whole point of M4. The other NINE met criteria are FALSE on measured
# dates, listed on each row below. RE-DERIVED 2026-08-21 from the committed file with rdflib,
# not counted by hand: of 11 `met true` dec criteria, 2 are retrospective TRUE (07, 10) and 9
# FALSE (01, 03, 04, 05, 06, 08, 11, 14, 16) — criterion 16 is the ninth, added under Ruling 12.
#
# NO LIVENESS CRITERION IS AUTHORED HERE (decision D3 of the plan). R99 (iladub:NoLeakShape
# has focus nodes but its body names iladub:asserted, which no compiled graph carries) and
# R100 (dec:EscalationShape live at document scope, idle at page scope) are about whether a
# shape ever FIRES where it is wired — a different question from CLAUDE.md:252's, which asks
# only whether the pairing exists. Both attach to `tab` criterion 10 in task 6. Neither
# un-meets a pairing criterion here, and no prog:blockedBy edge is authored on this rung.
#
# EVERY MET ROW'S ORACLES WERE RUN, not read, 2026-08-21:
#   $ ./.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/test_vocab_shapes.py tests/test_timeline_shacl.py \
#       tests/test_event_shacl.py tests/test_expansion_request.py \
#       tests/test_escalation_shacl.py tests/test_risk.py tests/test_governance.py \
#       tests/test_boundary.py tests/test_grounding.py -q
#     ............................................                            [100%]
#     44 passed in 1.55s
#
# NON-VACUITY OF THE POSITIVE HALF. "Ships a worked example that conforms" is vacuously true
# of an example with no focus node for the shape, so the focus nodes were counted (target
# class closed under rdfs:subClassOf from the ontology; targetObjectsOf/targetSubjectsOf
# counted directly), 2026-08-21 — every one of the sixteen has at least one:
#   DecisionHolon 1 · Confidence 1 · Milestone 1 · Event 1 · ExpansionRequest 1 ·
#   Escalation 2 · NoEmpiricRisk 5 · RiskAssessment 2 · Sensitivity 3 · AiInheritsUser 4 ·
#   Permission 7 · CandidateConcept 1 · GroundedNode 1 · PromotionDecision 1 · NoLeak 1 ·
#   HgaGroundingGovernance 1
# and the count is taken over EXACTLY the files each criterion cites, which is what caught
# criterion 10: iladub:NoLeakShape has 0 focus nodes in examples/promotion.ttl alone and 1
# across proposal.ttl + promotion.ttl, so the artifact list had to name both.

prog:rung:dec prog:criterion
    prog:criterion:dec:01 , prog:criterion:dec:02 , prog:criterion:dec:03 ,
    prog:criterion:dec:04 , prog:criterion:dec:05 , prog:criterion:dec:06 ,
    prog:criterion:dec:07 , prog:criterion:dec:08 , prog:criterion:dec:09 ,
    prog:criterion:dec:10 , prog:criterion:dec:11 , prog:criterion:dec:12 ,
    prog:criterion:dec:13 , prog:criterion:dec:14 , prog:criterion:dec:15 ,
    prog:criterion:dec:16 , prog:criterion:dec:17 .

