# --- the seventeenth: a rule in the Contract that no test asserts ------------------------
#
# CLAUDE.md:249-251 is a different rule from :252 and gets its own prog:source:
#   "- Decision/provenance reuse standards: `dec:DecisionHolon ⊑ prov:Activity`;
#      evidence via `prov:used`, agency via `prov:wasAssociatedWith`, products via
#      `prov:generated`. Don't reinvent provenance."
# All four axioms ARE on disk. MEASURED 2026-08-21, `sed -n '38p;55p;72p;85p' vocab/ontology/dec.ttl`:
#     rdfs:subClassOf prov:Activity ;
#     rdfs:subPropertyOf prov:used ;
#     rdfs:subPropertyOf prov:wasAssociatedWith ;
#     rdfs:subPropertyOf prov:generated ;
# And NO test asserts any of them. MEASURED 2026-08-21:
#   $ grep -rn "Activity" tests --include="*.py"
#     (no output; exit 1 — zero hits)
#   tests/test_hga_alignment.py:69-70 pins dec:partOf and dec:Event against HGA, and nothing
#   else in tests/ mentions prov:used, prov:generated or prov:wasAssociatedWith as an axiom.
# A rule declared in the Contract class and enforced by nothing is a hole, and this is the
# instrument's job: to make it countable rather than remembered.
#
# prog:declaredOn "2026-05-31". The `git log -L 249,251:CLAUDE.md` range reports FOUR commits
# (ee221de 2026-05-31, 965565b 2026-06-26, 0145138 2026-07-01, 84110a2 2026-07-01), but three
# of those are not touches to this rule — the range tracks line POSITIONS, and 965565b and
# 0145138 both edit the adjacent namespaces bullet while these three lines appear as unchanged
# context. The only edit to the rule itself is at 84110a2, which changes `hol:DecisionHolon`
# to `dec:DecisionHolon` and nothing else. A namespace rename is not a re-declaration (the
# same rule this manifest applies to the `holon` rung above), so the declaration is ee221de,
# 2026-05-31 — the day the Contract was written.
#
# NO prog:oracleArtifact here, deliberately — but NOT because naming one would be refused.
# On THIS row it would be inert: M5 evaluates only `met true` criteria
# (tests/test_arc_manifest.py:153-156), and this row is `met false`, so an artifact named here
# would be neither checked nor consulted. It is omitted because the moment someone flips this
# row to met, an existing vocab/ontology/dec.ttl would let M5 pass a claim that is still false
# — the axioms are on disk; the TEST is what is missing. Falsification arm A in task 4's
# report runs exactly that counterfactual and shows M5 silent and M5b alone refusing. Leaving
# the field off keeps the row's only evidence the one that can fail: prog:oracleTest.
prog:criterion:dec:17 a prog:Criterion ;
    prog:ofRung "dec" ;
    prog:statement "The four provenance-reuse axioms declared in the Contract — dec:DecisionHolon ⊑ prov:Activity, dec:consideredEvidence ⊑ prov:used, dec:decidedBy ⊑ prov:wasAssociatedWith, dec:produced ⊑ prov:generated (vocab/ontology/dec.ttl:38,55,72,85) — are asserted by a test. They are declared and enforced by nothing." ;
    prog:source "CLAUDE.md:249-251" ;
    prog:declaredOn "2026-05-31"^^xsd:date ;
    prog:met false ;
    prog:retrospective false ;
    prog:oracleTest "tests/test_hga_alignment.py::test_dec_provenance_axioms_present" .


# ========================================================================= tab — 10 criteria
#
# THE DENOMINATOR IS THE READING'S OWN VOCABULARY, not the residue register. Spec §7.4 states
# the trap first and it is worth restating: making each open `tab:` residue a criterion would
# put the numerator near zero on the rung carrying the majority of the repo's code, and would
# be measuring the register rather than the reading. So the nine criteria below are the nine
# reasons the compiler may refuse to read a region, plus a tenth for the compile membrane's
# own honesty (D3).
#
# THE REASON LIST IS A COPY OF A GREP, AND HERE IS THE GREP. There is no enum and no registry
# — the reasons exist only as string literals at `escalate_region(` call sites, deliberately:
# `_suggester_uri` (holon.py:409-421) slugifies the string rather than looking it up, its
# docstring giving the reason ("a hand-maintained table drifts from the call sites … and the
# drift is silent"). So this list can drift, and a manifest that carried it without its grep
# would be the hand-maintained table that docstring refuses to keep.
# RE-MEASURED 2026-08-21, this tree:
#   $ grep -rn "escalate_region(" src/ --include='*.py' | grep -v __pycache__
#     MULTI_TABLE_AMBIGUOUS  compile.py:596
#     REGION_TILING_FAILED   compile.py:656, :763, :939
#     TRANSPOSED             compile.py:688
#     ROW_GROUP_AMBIGUOUS    compile.py:739
#     MATRIX_AMBIGUOUS       compile.py:830
#     MERGE_AMBIGUOUS        compile.py:911
#     KIND_NOT_SUPPORTED     compile.py:978
#     DATAGRID_RESIDUE       compile.py:1145
#     ROUND_TRIP_FAIL        holon.py:493
# NINE, and the grep agrees exactly with the census (2026-08-20, HEAD 820ab24) — including
# that spec §7.4's EIGHT is wrong: it misfiles `TRANSPOSED` as a kind, and `RegionKind`
# (regions.py:27-30) has exactly three members, none of them TRANSPOSED. The tenth criterion
# is D3's, not a reason. (compile.py:961 carries a tenth *comment* mentioning the function and
# is not a call site — it states that ROUND_TRIP_FAIL never reaches escalate_region on that
# path. Counted as prose, not as a firing.)
#
# THE FIRING COUNTS ARE THE CENSUS'S, AND THE CENSUS IS STILL CURRENT. It ran at HEAD 820ab24
# and this manifest asserts against it rather than re-running a ~315 s corpus compile.
# That inheritance is checked, not assumed — MEASURED 2026-08-21:
#   $ git diff --stat 820ab24..HEAD -- src/ corpus/
#     (no output — src/ and corpus/ are byte-identical to the census HEAD)
# Per-reason, graph-side, over the 7-document corpus (census § Seam 1):
#   REGION_TILING_FAILED 10 · MATRIX_AMBIGUOUS 5 · ROUND_TRIP_FAIL 5 · KIND_NOT_SUPPORTED 3 ·
#   DATAGRID_RESIDUE 1 · MERGE_AMBIGUOUS 0 · MULTI_TABLE_AMBIGUOUS 0 · ROW_GROUP_AMBIGUOUS 0 ·
#   TRANSPOSED 0        — 24 records on 3 documents (apple 11, bfs 10, who-wfa 3).
#
# D2 — GRAPH-SIDE 24, REPORT-SIDE 29, AND THE DIFFERENCE IS ONE PAGE. Recorded here and not
# only in the plan, so a future re-measurement reading 29 recognises a known difference rather
# than drift. The delta is entirely apple page 1, the adopted page: 5 escalations are
# WITHDRAWN from the graph when the data grid supersedes them (document.py:1512-1513 ->
# `_remove_escalation_record`) while the RegionReport keeps its original reason
# (compile.py:1132-1136 rewrites only `verdict` and `tokens_escalated`). Withdrawn:
# REGION_TILING_FAILED x3, KIND_NOT_SUPPORTED x1, ROUND_TRIP_FAIL x1, replaced by one
# DATAGRID_RESIDUE. THIS MANIFEST COUNTS GRAPH-SIDE — a SHACL membrane over a compiled graph
# can only ever see the 24, and a criterion counting the other side would be uncheckable by
# the membrane that governs everything else here.
#
# ROUND_TRIP_FAIL IS TWO MECHANISMS UNDER ONE LABEL, and criterion 09 counts the label.
# Region-level (holon.py:493) accounts for all 5 corpus firings; cell-level
# (`_emit_roundtrip_fail_cell`, holon.py:55, called from :143, :210, :310, :405) is
# corpus-dead. A count keyed on the label alone cannot tell them apart, and one document
# hitting the cell-level path could inflate it by hundreds. WHETHER THE MANIFEST SHOULD SPLIT
# THEM INTO TWO CRITERIA IS DELIBERATELY LEFT OPEN — it is a real question about the shape of
# this denominator and it is not decided here rather than decided silently. What is asserted:
# criterion 09's `met false` does not depend on the answer, since the region-level half alone
# fires 5 times unadjudicated.
#
# D1 IS WHY THE FOUR CORPUS-DEAD REASONS ARE NOT AUTOMATICALLY MET (plan :91-97, which is
# every criterion 01-09's prog:source). Spec §7.4's one-armed wording would read all four as
# met for a reason that measures THE CORPUS, NOT THE READING — the same gameability defect as
# the `etkl` floor, from the other side. Under D1 a corpus-dead reason is disposed only if it
# names a COLLECTABLE oracle that drives the path AND a recorded reason distinguishing corpus
# gap from dead path. That is the VACUITY_REGISTRY form (test_vacuity_registry.py:87), which
# is the precedent already in this repo.
#
# WHAT A prog:blockedBy MEANS ON THIS RUNG, stated because it decided two rows: an edge names
# a register row WHOSE CLOSURE WOULD ADVANCE THIS CRITERION. It is not "a row that mentions
# this reason". R15 mentions MERGE_AMBIGUOUS and R68 is entirely about TRANSPOSED, yet neither
# is an edge below — both are the RECORDED REASON D1 arm (b) asks for, and closing them would
# not dispose of anything. All edges below re-verified OPEN 2026-08-21:
#   $ grep -nE "^\| *~?~?R(43|44|45|62|71|74|77|79|80|83|84|97|98|99|100)~?~? *\|" \
#         docs/superpowers/residues.md
#     all fifteen present, all `| open |`, none struck.
#
# ONE STALE REGISTER ROW FOUND AND NOT FIXED HERE. R43 reads "ONS gov-stats document: 1x
# REGION_TILING_FAILED plus an unnamed oddity", and the census measures ons at ZERO escalation
# records of any reason (§ Seam 1). The row is open, so M7 admits the edge and criterion 02
# keeps it; but the occurrence it describes does not survive at HEAD, exactly as
# graincorp-stem's 2026-08-02 adjudication did not (task 5 superseded that one in
# tests/corpus-manifest.ttl:43-44). Re-adjudicating R43 is register work, not manifest work,
# and inventing a closure for it here would be this loop marking its own homework.
#
# ALL TEN CARRY prog:declaredOn "2026-08-20" — f436a8c, the commit that authored the plan.
# MEASURED 2026-08-21:
#   $ git blame -L 91,97 --date=short -- docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-20-the-arc-has-a-denominator.md
#     f436a8c3 (2026-08-20) for every line of D1's decision block
#   $ git blame -L 129,131 --date=short -- <same file>
#     f436a8c3 (2026-08-20) for every line of D3's decision block
# This is the one rung §7 says had to be CONSTRUCTED rather than read off prose that predates
# it, so its declaring prose is this loop's own plan and its date is that plan's commit — not
# today's. The distinction is not cosmetic: writing today's date would make every row look
# declared after the evidence was already in hand.
#
# NON-VACUITY OF EVERY NAMED ORACLE, checked BY HAND (the rule at :561-571 generalises to this
# rung, and nothing enforces it — R106). Each of the four corpus-dead reasons' oracles was RUN
# and READ, 2026-08-21:
#   $ ./.venv/bin/python -m pytest \
#       "tests/etkl/test_merge_resolution.py::test_offcenter_merge_escalates" \
#       "tests/etkl/test_closing_slice.py::test_multi_table_ambiguous_escalates" \
#       "tests/etkl/test_closing_slice.py::test_false_positive_transpose_escalates" \
#       "tests/etkl/test_tiling_gate.py::test_gate_reject_escalates_gracefully" -q
#     4 passed in 4.67s
# Three of the four assert GRAPH-SIDE — over `iladub:CandidateConcept` subjects carrying
# `rdfs:label = <reason>`, which only `escalate_region` writes (holon.py:450-463) — so an
# empty escalation set fails the assertion rather than satisfying it vacuously. The fourth
# (ROW_GROUP_AMBIGUOUS) asserts report-side on `r.verdict == "escalated" and r.reason ==
# "ROW_GROUP_AMBIGUOUS"`, which is equally falsifiable by absence. The one MET row's oracle was
# falsified for real: inverting the reason literal at compile.py:911 makes
# test_offcenter_merge_escalates FAIL (task 6 report, FALSIFICATION arm B).

prog:rung:tab prog:criterion
    prog:criterion:tab:01 , prog:criterion:tab:02 , prog:criterion:tab:03 ,
    prog:criterion:tab:04 , prog:criterion:tab:05 , prog:criterion:tab:06 ,
    prog:criterion:tab:07 , prog:criterion:tab:08 , prog:criterion:tab:09 ,
    prog:criterion:tab:10 .

# --- the nine escalation reasons, in call-site order ------------------------------------
#
# The five FIRING reasons (01 is not one of them) share a shape: arm (a) applies, every firing
# document's task-5 adjudication NAMES the reason, and every one of those adjudications is a
# recorded HOLD rather than a disposition. Naming is not disposing, so all five read
# `met false` — and each also carries open blocking edges, which M8 makes binding.
# Their prog:oracleTest is a TARGET on every one of the five, and the same target, deliberately:
# `cor:` has NO per-reason disposal term today, so "this reason is disposed on this document"
# is not a structural fact any test can read — it lives in a rationale string, and the `etkl`
# leg's own lesson (tests/test_arc_manifest.py::etkl_met_by_document's docstring) is that a predicate must never read a
# rationale. WHETHER `cor:` SHOULD GAIN SUCH A TERM IS LEFT OPEN, and is named here rather
# than decided silently. Until it does, the target names where the proof would have to live.

# CORPUS-DEAD (0 firings). BLOCKED: R74 measures the cbh data grid leaking one row from a
# SECOND table on the same page — which is this reason's exact subject matter, and therefore
# a corpus place where its silence may be FALSE silence rather than absence. Closing R74 is
# what would let arm (b) speak.
prog:criterion:tab:01 a prog:Criterion ;
    prog:ofRung "tab" ;
    prog:statement "MULTI_TABLE_AMBIGUOUS (compile.py:596): this escalation reason is disposed — either it fires on the 7-document corpus and every firing document carries a dated cor:adjudication naming and disposing of it, or it fires nowhere on the corpus and names a collectable prog:oracleTest that exercises the path, plus a recorded reason distinguishing corpus gap from dead path." ;
    prog:source "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-20-the-arc-has-a-denominator.md:91-97" ;
    prog:declaredOn "2026-08-20"^^xsd:date ;
    prog:met false ;
    prog:retrospective false ;
    prog:blockedBy "R74" ;
    prog:oracleTest "tests/etkl/test_closing_slice.py::test_multi_table_ambiguous_escalates" .

# FIRES 10 — apple x8 (p0 x4, p2 x4), bfs x2 (p4, p5). Both documents' 2026-08-20 adjudications
# name it; both HOLD. R43 is the stale row noted in this section's header.
prog:criterion:tab:02 a prog:Criterion ;
    prog:ofRung "tab" ;
    prog:statement "REGION_TILING_FAILED (compile.py:656, :763, :939): this escalation reason is disposed — either it fires on the 7-document corpus and every firing document carries a dated cor:adjudication naming and disposing of it, or it fires nowhere on the corpus and names a collectable prog:oracleTest that exercises the path, plus a recorded reason distinguishing corpus gap from dead path." ;
    prog:source "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-20-the-arc-has-a-denominator.md:91-97" ;
    prog:declaredOn "2026-08-20"^^xsd:date ;
    prog:met false ;
    prog:retrospective false ;
    prog:blockedBy "R43" , "R44" , "R62" ;
    prog:oracleTest "tests/test_corpus.py::test_escalation_reasons_are_adjudicated" .

# CORPUS-DEAD (0 firings) AND THE SILENCE IS SUPPRESSED, WHICH IS A THIRD STATE. The brief said
# spec §7.4's table gives this reason no blocking row and told this task to MEASURE whether one
# exists. Two do, and they are different in kind:
#   * R68 — "no real corpus document exercises the transposed path … proven only on synthetic
#     fixtures". That is D1 arm (b)'s RECORDED REASON, corpus gap, not a blocker. Closing it
#     (a genuinely transposing document entering the corpus) would move this row to arm (a),
#     not meet it.
#   * R71 — "the kind gate is load-bearing: suppressing `looks_transposed` on an
#     UNSUPPORTED_TABLE band is currently the only thing protecting two stem regions from a
#     false-positive transposition reading", and the row measures that un-gating routes both
#     bands to the incoherent branch, WHICH ESCALATES AT 0 CELLS. So this reason's corpus zero
#     is not "the reading never meets a transposed table" — it is "the reading meets two bands
#     it would call transposed, and a gate the register flags as an unresolved defect
#     suppresses that reading." Neither corpus gap nor dead path. BLOCKED on R71.
prog:criterion:tab:03 a prog:Criterion ;
    prog:ofRung "tab" ;
    prog:statement "TRANSPOSED (compile.py:688): this escalation reason is disposed — either it fires on the 7-document corpus and every firing document carries a dated cor:adjudication naming and disposing of it, or it fires nowhere on the corpus and names a collectable prog:oracleTest that exercises the path, plus a recorded reason distinguishing corpus gap from dead path." ;
    prog:source "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-20-the-arc-has-a-denominator.md:91-97" ;
    prog:declaredOn "2026-08-20"^^xsd:date ;
    prog:met false ;
    prog:retrospective false ;
    prog:blockedBy "R71" ;
    prog:oracleTest "tests/etkl/test_closing_slice.py::test_false_positive_transpose_escalates" .

# CORPUS-DEAD (0 firings). BLOCKED: R80 (apple p1's indent hierarchy is read by nobody), R74
# (the cbh leaked row), R77 (cbh's four panel totals missed for the no-label reason) — three
# corpus places where row-group structure goes unread WITHOUT this reason firing. Its oracle
# reaches the path only by monkeypatching `tiling.region_tiles` to reject, which is honest and
# is stated here: no fixture drives ROW_GROUP_AMBIGUOUS through the live oracle.
prog:criterion:tab:04 a prog:Criterion ;
    prog:ofRung "tab" ;
