# THE ONE MET ROW ON THIS RUNG, and it is met on arm (b), never on silence.
#   * fires nowhere: census § Seam 1, 0 on all 7 documents;
#   * names a collectable oracle that DRIVES the path: test_offcenter_merge_escalates compiles
#     `fixtures.offcenter_merge_report_pdf` and asserts, graph-side, that a CandidateConcept
#     carries rdfs:label "MERGE_AMBIGUOUS" — a label only escalate_region writes — AND that no
#     tab:HierarchicalTable was asserted. Run 2026-08-21, passed; falsified by inverting the
#     reason literal at compile.py:911 (task 6 report);
#   * recorded reason distinguishing corpus gap from dead path: R15, open — "still escalates
#     honestly MERGE_AMBIGUOUS" (the path is LIVE) and "No measured document needs it" / "if a
#     real document ever requires it" (the gap is the CORPUS). Both halves in one row.
# NO BLOCKING EDGE, and that is measured rather than assumed. R6 (centre-only merge candidate)
# and R8 (ProposeHeaderSpan missing from baml_src/) both touch merge reading; neither records a
# corpus place where this reason's silence is false. R6's own "where measured" column says
# "needs a live run to judge" — an unmeasured row is not evidence of false silence — and R8 is
# about the NEURAL proposer that would RESOLVE an ambiguity, not about one going unseen.
# prog:retrospective TRUE, and M4 refuses `false` outright: the oracle and R15 both predate
# 2026-08-20, so this criterion was written against evidence that already existed and was met
# the moment it was declared. metOn == declaredOn. Grandfathering is labelled, never hidden —
# and back-dating declaredOn or forward-dating metOn to dodge that label is the move M4 exists
# to catch.
prog:criterion:tab:06 a prog:Criterion ;
    prog:ofRung "tab" ;
    prog:statement "MERGE_AMBIGUOUS (compile.py:911): this escalation reason is disposed — either it fires on the 7-document corpus and every firing document carries a dated cor:adjudication naming and disposing of it, or it fires nowhere on the corpus and names a collectable prog:oracleTest that exercises the path, plus a recorded reason distinguishing corpus gap from dead path." ;
    prog:source "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-20-the-arc-has-a-denominator.md:91-97" ;
    prog:declaredOn "2026-08-20"^^xsd:date ;
    prog:met true ;
    prog:metOn "2026-08-20"^^xsd:date ;
    prog:retrospective true ;
    prog:oracleArtifact "tests/etkl/fixtures.py:726" ;
    prog:oracleTest "tests/etkl/test_merge_resolution.py::test_offcenter_merge_escalates" .

